Dallas <snakesbloodpussycat@yahoo.com> writes:

> has said that spending time on cleared levels is not necessary and
> inadvisable, but there is no outright penalty for doing so.

When you enter a new level, there are many items generated with the
level, some of them possibly useful to you.
When you stay on one level, the only items getting generated are those
generated in monsters' inventory and death drops. But monsters get
generated as much on other levels where you go.
So, exploring new levels is more likely to generate useful items than
staying on a level you have already fully explored. That's why it is not
a good idea to stay too long on one level if there is no reason to do it
(like healing from your wounds on a cleared level, using an altar or
something else).

